  "title": "epan: Prevent undefined behavior in compute_offset",
  "description": "With 2's complement integers, taking the negation of a INT_MIN\nis technically undefined behavior, even though in practice all\ncompilers will produce the expected result if doing so and then\ncasting to an unsigned. (The two's complement of INT_MIN is INT_MIN\nitself; casting to an unsigned yields INT_MIN + UINT_MAX + 1 = -INT_MAX\nas desired.)\n\nExpressing the unary minus plus cast in a slightly more complicated\nmanner (adding 1 both before and after negating) produces the same\nresult but avoids the undefined behavior. All known compilers\n(GCC, Clang, MSVC) recognize this and optimize to the expected single\ninstruction on all architectures, according to godbolt.org\n\nFix #20707",
